-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c321af2-89cb-566e-af68-2679df6bf542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y)=x y + x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713106} {:answer/id #uuid "352a4493-7aa8-56d0-9a69-62558ee40f7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y)=x y - x + 3 y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713113} {:answer/id #uuid "5e6263fa-5281-5188-91b3-ef49cde0e887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y)=- x y + x - 3 y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713116} {:answer/id #uuid "c90c46ae-b7df-5f24-ac82-4ab497ecbc40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y)=- x y + x + 3 y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713127} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ece84e-5fae-5082-996a-fcbc622b0fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y)=- x y + 3 y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "352a4493-7aa8-56d0-9a69-62558ee40f7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y)=x y - x + 3 y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713113} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f35954a-67b7-5456-8f56-b7bfb1e59264" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ee1930f1-572a-55d9-8436-0d469eb78bb1" :question/problem "Find the general form of $f(x,y)$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla f={}&\\bigl(y - 1\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i\\\\\n&+\\bigl(x + 3\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWork on $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\nIn the choices, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "The vector components are $f_x$ and $f_y$. Integrate the first component with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as constant. Retain an arbitrary function $g(y)$ because its $x$-derivative is zero.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x,y)&=\\int\\bigl(y - 1\\bigr)\\,\\mathrm dx\\\\\n&=x y - x+g(y).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate with respect to $y$ and match the second component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y&=x+g'(y)\\\\\ng'(y)&=\\bigl(x + 3\\bigr)\\\\\n&\\quad-\\bigl(x\\bigr)\\\\\n&=3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function of $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ng(y)&=\\int\\bigl(3\\bigr)\\,\\mathrm dy\\\\\n&=3 y+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute to obtain\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=x y - x + 3 y+C\n$$\n\nBoth components check:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x&=y - 1,\\\\\nf_y&=x + 3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713142 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f3265cd-2b3d-518d-8bcb-b5d898370cfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)&=x^{2} y - 2 x^{2} - 2 x y^{2}\\\\&- \\sin{\\left(x + y \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713141} {:answer/id #uuid "54abd8ef-e462-54c3-9c7d-ce329db9275a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)&=x^{2} y + 2 x^{2} - 2 x y^{2}\\\\&- \\sin{\\left(x + y \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713150} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b4e29d-add7-588f-b1b6-943c7129e389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)&=x^{2} y + 2 x^{2} - 2 x y^{2}\\\\&+\\sin{\\left(x + y \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713161} {:answer/id #uuid "bd836ae6-be3c-5f1e-9a00-c7889d94333a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)&=- x^{2} y - 2 x^{2} - 2 x y^{2}\\\\&+\\sin{\\left(x + y \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713162} {:answer/id #uuid "ea15fdd6-1782-5fc4-8d84-7a3fcc8047ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)&=- x^{2} y + 2 x^{2} + 2 x y^{2}\\\\&- \\sin{\\left(x + y \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f3265cd-2b3d-518d-8bcb-b5d898370cfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)&=x^{2} y - 2 x^{2} - 2 x y^{2}\\\\&- \\sin{\\left(x + y \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713141} :answer-field/id #uuid "72db3735-8a37-5693-b45c-c2794dd8eb6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "110d1a04-5b07-5a37-8345-9bfa499ee728" :question/problem "Find the general form of $f(x,y)$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla f={}&\\bigl(2 x y - 4 x - 2 y^{2} - \\cos{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i\\\\\n&+\\bigl(x^{2} - 4 x y - \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWork on $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\nIn the choices, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "The vector components are $f_x$ and $f_y$. Integrate the first component with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as constant. Retain an arbitrary function $g(y)$ because its $x$-derivative is zero.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x,y)&=\\int\\bigl(2 x y - 4 x - 2 y^{2} - \\cos{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\bigr)\\,\\mathrm dx\\\\\n&=x^{2} y - 2 x^{2} - 2 x y^{2} - \\sin{\\left(x + y \\right)}+g(y).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate with respect to $y$ and match the second component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y&=x^{2} - 4 x y - \\cos{\\left(x + y \\right)}+g'(y)\\\\\ng'(y)&=\\bigl(x^{2} - 4 x y - \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\bigr)\\\\\n&\\quad-\\bigl(x^{2} - 4 x y - \\cos{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\bigr)\\\\\n&=- \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function of $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ng(y)&=\\int\\bigl(- \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\\bigr)\\,\\mathrm dy\\\\\n&=\\cos{\\left(y \\right)}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)&=x^{2} y - 2 x^{2} - 2 x y^{2}\\\\&- \\sin{\\left(x + y \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth components check:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x&=2 x y - 4 x - 2 y^{2} - \\cos{\\left(x + y \\right)},\\\\\nf_y&=x^{2} - 4 x y - \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(x + y \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713149 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17d753a1-f088-5dd8-a8c1-8da8330759da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)&=x^{2} y - x y^{2}\\\\&+e^{x y}+C\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713144} {:answer/id #uuid "7d12a1fd-2820-517d-aed1-ea7da339e713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)&=x^{2} y + x y^{2}\\\\&+e^{x y} - \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713157} {:answer/id #uuid "a812b66a-e2d8-5dec-98a4-8ddd3c01e2a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)&=- x^{2} y - x y^{2}\\\\&- e^{x y}+C\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713159} {:answer/id #uuid "e4a4e4cd-178d-5100-9442-3e88a9cb9999" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)&=x^{2} y + x^{2} - x y^{2}\\\\&+e^{x y} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713165} {:answer/id #uuid "ee8f117a-2229-557c-a938-f91c1565074f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860