 #edb/ref 17592186713146} :answer-field/id #uuid "28da96bb-f158-55f4-809a-9c934ed420a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "aebe6773-78d2-5685-abb5-35e9245d2f57" :question/problem "Find the general form of $f(x,y)$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla f={}&\\bigl(- 4 x y - 4 x + y^{2} - y e^{x y}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i\\\\\n&+\\bigl(- 2 x^{2} + 2 x y - x e^{x y} - \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWork on $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\nIn the choices, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "The vector components are $f_x$ and $f_y$. Integrate the first component with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as constant. Retain an arbitrary function $g(y)$ because its $x$-derivative is zero.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x,y)&=\\int\\bigl(- 4 x y - 4 x + y^{2} - y e^{x y}\\bigr)\\,\\mathrm dx\\\\\n&=- 2 x^{2} y - 2 x^{2} + x y^{2} - e^{x y}+g(y).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate with respect to $y$ and match the second component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y&=- 2 x^{2} + 2 x y - x e^{x y}+g'(y)\\\\\ng'(y)&=\\bigl(- 2 x^{2} + 2 x y - x e^{x y} - \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\\bigr)\\\\\n&\\quad-\\bigl(- 2 x^{2} + 2 x y - x e^{x y}\\bigr)\\\\\n&=- \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function of $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ng(y)&=\\int\\bigl(- \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\\bigr)\\,\\mathrm dy\\\\\n&=\\cos{\\left(y \\right)}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)&=- 2 x^{2} y - 2 x^{2} + x y^{2}\\\\&- e^{x y} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth components check:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x&=- 4 x y - 4 x + y^{2} - y e^{x y},\\\\\nf_y&=- 2 x^{2} + 2 x y - x e^{x y} - \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713168 :question/answer-field